---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import LegalSubnav from '../components/LegalSubnav.astro';
import { getSite } from '../lib/site';

const { privacyEmail, legalEmail } = getSite();

const description =
  'Bycon Privacy Policy — how we collect, use, disclose, and protect information in connection with the Transport Management System, websites, and related services, including SMS.';
---
<Layout title="Privacy Policy" description={description}>
  <article class="prose privacy-doc">
    <LegalSubnav current="privacy" />

    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="effective-date"><strong>Effective date:</strong> March 29, 2026</p>

    <p>
      This Privacy Policy describes how <strong>Bycon</strong> (“we,” “us,” or “our”) collects, uses, discloses, and protects
      information in connection with the Transport Management System and related services (the “Services”), including when
      we send you text messages. By using the Services or providing your information to us, you agree to this Policy unless
      a separate agreement states otherwise.
    </p>

    <section class="privacy-section" id="collect" aria-labelledby="h-collect">
      <h2 id="h-collect">1. Information we collect</h2>
      <p>We may collect the following categories of information, depending on how you use the Services:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Contact and identity data:</strong> name, email address, phone number, mailing address, employer or
          contracting organization, and similar identifiers.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Account and authentication data:</strong> usernames, credentials, role, and security-related information.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Transportation and operations data:</strong> schedules, trips, routes, pickup and drop-off information,
          vehicle or driver assignments, timesheets, and related operational records needed to provide transportation or
          workforce management.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Communications:</strong> messages you send us, call or support logs, and records of SMS or other
          notifications we send (including delivery status where available).
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Device and technical data:</strong> IP address, browser or app version, device type, general location
          derived from IP, and cookies or similar technologies when you use our websites or apps.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="privacy-section" id="use" aria-labelledby="h-use">
      <h2 id="h-use">2. How we use information</h2>
      <p>We use information to:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Provide, operate, maintain, and improve the Services;</li>
        <li>Schedule and coordinate transportation and related workforce activities;</li>
        <li>
          Send transactional, operational, and service-related messages (including SMS) such as trip updates, reminders, and
          security notices;
        </li>
        <li>Respond to inquiries, provide support, and enforce our terms;</li>
        <li>Protect the security and integrity of our systems and users;</li>
        <li>Comply with law, regulatory requirements, and lawful requests; and</li>
        <li>
          With appropriate consent where required, send marketing or promotional communications (you may opt out as described
          in those messages or below).
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="privacy-section" id="sms" aria-labelledby="h-sms">
      <h2 id="h-sms">3. Text messages (SMS)</h2>
      <p>
        If you opt in to receive text messages from us, we will use your mobile number to send the types of messages
        described at the point of opt-in (for example, trip notifications or account alerts). Message frequency varies based
        on your use of the Services and your preferences.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Charges:</strong> Message and data rates may apply according to your carrier plan. Carriers are not liable
        for delayed or undelivered messages.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Opt-out:</strong> You may opt out of promotional SMS at any time by following the instructions in the message
        (e.g., replying STOP). For transactional or legally required messages, we may still send certain notices as permitted
        by law or until your relationship with us ends; contact us if you have questions.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Help:</strong> Reply HELP for assistance or contact us at{' '}
        <a href={`mailto:${legalEmail}`}>{legalEmail}</a>.
      </p>
      <p>
        We do not sell your phone number or use it for unrelated third-party marketing without your consent where such
        consent is required.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="privacy-section" id="share" aria-labelledby="h-share">
      <h2 id="h-share">4. How we share information</h2>
      <p>We may share information with:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Service providers</strong> who assist us (e.g., hosting, messaging/SMS delivery, mapping, analytics,
          customer support) under contractual obligations to protect data;
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Transportation partners or your organization,</strong> where necessary to deliver the Services you or they
          have requested;
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Legal and safety:</strong> when required by law, court order, or government request, or when we believe
          disclosure is necessary to protect rights, safety, or security;
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Business transfers:</strong> in connection with a merger, acquisition, or sale of assets, subject to
          appropriate safeguards.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>We do not sell personal information as the term “sale” is commonly defined in U.S. state privacy laws.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="privacy-section" id="retention" aria-labelledby="h-retention">
      <h2 id="h-retention">5. Retention</h2>
      <p>
        We retain information for as long as needed to provide the Services, meet legal, tax, and accounting obligations,
        resolve disputes, and enforce our agreements. Retention periods may vary by data type and jurisdiction.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="privacy-section" id="security" aria-labelledby="h-security">
      <h2 id="h-security">6. Security</h2>
      <p>
        We implement reasonable technical and organizational measures designed to protect personal information. No method of
        transmission or storage is completely secure; we cannot guarantee absolute security.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="privacy-section" id="rights" aria-labelledby="h-rights">
      <h2 id="h-rights">7. Your choices and rights</h2>
      <p>
        Depending on where you live, you may have rights to access, correct, delete, or restrict certain processing of your
        personal information, or to object to or opt out of certain uses. To exercise applicable rights, contact us at the
        email below. We may verify your request as permitted by law.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="privacy-section" id="children" aria-labelledby="h-children">
      <h2 id="h-children">8. Children’s privacy</h2>
      <p>
        The Services are not directed to children under 13 (or the age required in your jurisdiction). We do not knowingly
        collect personal information from children in violation of applicable law.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="privacy-section" id="international" aria-labelledby="h-international">
      <h2 id="h-international">9. International users</h2>
      <p>
        If you access the Services from outside the country where we operate, your information may be processed in
        countries that may not provide the same level of data protection as your home country. Where required, we use
        appropriate safeguards.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="privacy-section" id="changes" aria-labelledby="h-changes">
      <h2 id="h-changes">10. Changes to this Policy</h2>
      <p>
        We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. We will post the updated version with a revised effective date
        and, where appropriate, provide additional notice (such as email or an in-app message).
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="privacy-section" id="contact" aria-labelledby="h-contact">
      <h2 id="h-contact">11. Contact us</h2>
      <p>
        For questions about this Privacy Policy or our data practices, contact Bycon at{' '}
        <a href={`mailto:${legalEmail}`}>{legalEmail}</a>
        {legalEmail !== privacyEmail ? (
          <>
            . You may also reach our privacy team at <a href={`mailto:${privacyEmail}`}>{privacyEmail}</a>.
          </>
        ) : (
          '.'
        )}
      </p>
    </section>

    <p class="privacy-footnote">
      This policy is provided for general information and does not constitute legal advice. You may wish to have it reviewed
      by counsel for your organization and jurisdiction.
    </p>
  </article>

  <style>
    .privacy-doc {
      max-width: 42rem;
    }
    .effective-date {
      font-size: 0.9375rem;
      color: var(--muted);
      margin: 0 0 1.25rem;
    }
    .privacy-section h2 {
      font-size: 1.125rem;
      font-weight: 600;
      margin: 1.75rem 0 0.5rem;
      scroll-margin-top: 4rem;
    }
    .privacy-footnote {
      font-size: 0.8125rem;
      color: var(--muted);
      margin-top: 2rem;
      padding-top: 1.25rem;
      border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
    }
  </style>
</Layout>
